# Deployment & Tenancy

**Default delivery (ADR 005):** shared SaaS — one app deployment, one PostgreSQL, **`tenant_id`** row isolation.

|          | SaaS (default)              | Independent deploy (deferred) |
| -------- | --------------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| App      | Shared API process(es)      | One Docker stack per buyer    |
| DB       | Shared PG + `tenant_id`     | PG per buyer                  |
| Signup   | Self-service trial → tenant | Manual provision per buyer    |
| Billing  | Subscription (`status`)     | Per-deploy contract           |
| Language | User picker (`zh-TW` \| `en`); tenant `locale` is default only | Same picker; YAML `locale` is default only |

## Tenant lifecycle

```text
signup → tenant (trial) + owner → trial_ends_at → subscribe → active | suspended
```

Payment integration deferred; manual status updates OK initially.

## Tenant record

`tenants`: `slug`, `edition`, `modules`, `locale`, `dashboard_layout`, `status`, `trial_ends_at`.

Onboarding copies from `deploy/presets/personal.yaml` or `professional.yaml`. **`deploy/config.yaml`** is local dev bootstrap only (single-tenant until tenant-backed config ships).

## Resolution

JWT carries `tenant_id`; auth deps scope all queries. Subdomain routing optional later.

## Out of scope / deferred

- Fleet (same image, N stacks + N PG) — optional data-sovereignty / on-prem tier later
- Multi-DB import (N buyer PGs → one PG) — out of scope (no independent-deploy buyers)
- Import from other databases into SaaS — cancelled; tenants start empty via signup
